  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Come in, take a seat. The nurse has had a quick word and says you're here about your hair, but I'd rather hear it in your own words.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:00",
      "end_timestamp": "00:13",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yeah. It's thinning.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:15",
      "end_timestamp": "00:17",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Thinning where, would you say? All over, or in one patch?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:19",
      "end_timestamp": "00:25",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "The top, mostly. The crown, where my parting is.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:27",
      "end_timestamp": "00:32",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And how long have you noticed it for?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:34",
      "end_timestamp": "00:38",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Six months. About that.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:41",
      "end_timestamp": "00:43",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Right. Is it more that hairs are falling out, or that they're getting finer so you can see more scalp through them?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:08",
      "end_timestamp": "01:19",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Both, a bit. It's coming out in handfuls when I wash it.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:22",
      "end_timestamp": "01:29",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Handfuls in the shower. Is that every wash, or just now and then?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:30",
      "end_timestamp": "01:37",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Every wash.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:38",
      "end_timestamp": "01:40",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Before anything else, a blood test makes sense. I'd like to check your iron stores and your thyroid, because both can quietly affect hair and both are easy to put right.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:01",
      "end_timestamp": "03:18",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "The nurse can take it on your way out today. It's about two minutes with a needle, no fasting needed.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:26",
      "end_timestamp": "03:38",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Meanwhile I'm going to start you on minoxidil foam. Carrying on with the lawn idea, it's a bit like fertiliser: it wakes the follicles up and lengthens their growing phase.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:42",
      "end_timestamp": "03:57",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Dry scalp is best. Once a day, half a capful, rubbed in wherever it's thin, then wash your hands thoroughly.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:03",
      "end_timestamp": "04:15",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Be warned, it can make you shed a bit more for the first month or so. That's the old resting hairs making way, and it's a good sign rather than a bad one.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:20",
      "end_timestamp": "04:37",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "A little worse first, yes. Most people need around four months before they see any difference, so please don't judge it too early.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:44",
      "end_timestamp": "04:56",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Take a photo of your crown in the same light today, and then again every month. It's far more reliable than trusting your memory in the bathroom mirror.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:00",
      "end_timestamp": "05:18",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And be kind to what you've got: no harsh brushing or tight hats. Ordinary shampoo is fine, you don't need anything fancy.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:24",
      "end_timestamp": "05:36",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[3]"
      ]
    }
  ],
